@* SPEC:  docs/00-COMPONENTS/2.7/05-LipiToast-Spec.md §6
   PHASE: 2.7 — Feedback Components
   AMEND: docs/CHANGE-LOG.md A35

   Toast renderer host. Placed once in TopNavLayout.razor (sibling to
   LipiOverlayHost). Subscribes to ILipiToastService.OnChanged and re-renders
   on state change.

   Layout: groups active toasts by Position (6 possible corners), renders
   one stack per corner that has toasts. Empty corners render nothing.

   File pattern (per Phase 2.7 BUILD-CHAT-HANDOFF literal):
     LipiToastHost.razor      — markup
     LipiToastHost.razor.cs   — partial class (subscription lifecycle)

   No scoped CSS file — corner positioning is in this markup via class names,
   and the toast surface CSS is in LipiToast.razor.css. Corner-position rules
   are in App.razor's global stylesheet expectation (none new); we use inline
   class-based selectors below with the host's own styling via a small block
   in this .razor file's @section if needed. (Final approach: rely on top-level
   positioning classes that are universally understood — no separate CSS file.)

   Decision: inline a small <style> block here at the top of the file so the
   global positioning rules ship with the host without needing a new css file.
   This keeps deploy-script entries minimal AND avoids cluttering wwwroot.
*@

@namespace LiPi.Web.Components.Shared
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@implements IDisposable
@using LiPi.Web.Services

@inject ILipiToastService ToastService

<style>
    /* ============================================================== */
    /* LipiToastHost — corner stack positioning                       */
    /* Inline style block instead of a separate .razor.css/.css file:  */
    /*   1. Fewer deploy-script entries to maintain                    */
    /*   2. Positions are short, well-defined, unlikely to grow        */
    /*   3. Host is a singleton in TopNavLayout — no scope concerns    */
    /*                                                                  */
    /* Stacks use pointer-events:none so they don't block clicks on    */
    /* page content. Individual .lipi-toast elements opt back in via   */
    /* pointer-events:auto in LipiToast.razor.css.                     */
    /* ============================================================== */

    .lipi-toast-host-stack {
        position: fixed;
        z-index: 900;                /* above LipiOverlayHost backdrop (799) and overlays (800-) */
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 8px;
        padding: 16px;
        pointer-events: none;
        max-width: 100vw;
    }

    .lipi-toast-host-top-right    { top: 0;    right: 0;  align-items: flex-end;   }
    .lipi-toast-host-top-center   { top: 0;    left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); align-items: center; }
    .lipi-toast-host-top-left     { top: 0;    left: 0;   align-items: flex-start; }
    .lipi-toast-host-bottom-right { bottom: 0; right: 0;  align-items: flex-end;   flex-direction: column-reverse; }
    .lipi-toast-host-bottom-center{ bottom: 0; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); align-items: center; flex-direction: column-reverse; }
    .lipi-toast-host-bottom-left  { bottom: 0; left: 0;   align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column-reverse; }
</style>

@foreach (var grp in GroupedByPosition)
{
    <div class="lipi-toast-host-stack @PositionClass(grp.Key)" aria-label="Notifications">
        @foreach (var entry in grp.Value)
        {
            <LipiToast @key="entry.Id"
                       Entry="entry"
                       OnDismissRequested="HandleDismiss"
                       OnActionInvoked="HandleAction" />
        }
    </div>
}
